{
 "answer": "The available regulatory sources do not address requirements for maintaining records of consumer complaints or adverse events, retention periods for such records, a written complaint-handling SOP, or mandatory investigation of every complaint for an indie brand under 21 CFR 71.15.\n\nAdverse reaction reports, product experience reports, and consumer complaints are considered confidential data in color additive petitions and may be redacted to remove names and any information that would identify the person using the product or a third party involved with the report [4](i), [4](ii).  \n\nNo retention period is specified for these records in 21 CFR 71.15.  \n\nThere is no requirement under 21 CFR 71.15 for an indie brand to maintain a written complaint-handling SOP or to investigate every complaint.  \n\n[4]\nThe retrieved evidence does not establish the time period or frequency asked for.",
